Date: Wed, 29 Apr 2026 23:29:10 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] phlink: phase 10.01a: update protocol spec (TUF v1.0.32
 subset)

Authors docs/dev/update-protocol.md, the on-the-wire contract between
phlink and the update CDN. Locks:

- TUF v1.0.32 subset (no delegated targets, no hash agility, no TAP-4).
- Ed25519-only, SHA-256-only, boringssl-backed.
- Four standard roles (root/targets/snapshot/timestamp), thresholds
  m=2/n=3 for root, m=1 for the rest.
- Static-file CDN at https://updates.phlink.dev/, single 'stable'
  channel for v1.0 alpha.
- Canonical-JSON re-emission on the client (don't trust server bytes).
- Verification staircase: timestamp -> snapshot (length+hash gated)
  -> targets (version gated).
- Threat model coverage: MITM, rollback, freeze, mix-and-match,
  online-key compromise, CDN compromise, endless-data, slowloris.
- Quarterly key rotation cadence; root only on compromise or expiry.
- Privacy: no install id, no telemetry, no cookies, no query params,
  User-Agent only.
- Failure logging: local-only, 1 MB rotated update.log per platform.

Foundation deliverable for Phase 10 plan 10-01. C++ TufClient skeleton
(in-tree, boringssl + base::JSONReader + SimpleURLLoader, no Rust
crate vendoring -- see Phase 10 CONTEXT D-01 pivot rationale) lands
in 10-01b.
